    "summary": "High‑energy autumn ’71 set with monster Other One jam",
    "blurb": "The band rolls through a tight first half and launches into an expansive second set highlighted by a 21‑minute The Other One suite. Jerry’s lead work shines on Playing In The Band and Tennessee Jed, while Keith’s keyboards dominate the mix. Overall a loose but inspired performance despite some muffled audio.",
    "review": "The October 29 show at Cleveland's Allan Theater captures the Dead in full autumnal stride. After a solid first set that includes bright renditions of El Paso, Playing In The Band and Tennessee Jed, the band dives into a sprawling second‑set adventure. A thunderous 21‑minute excursion through The Other One (bookended by Cryptical Envelopment) showcases tight interplay between Jerry’s ripping guitar and Phil’s anchoring bass, with Keith’s organ/piano driving the momentum from the front of the mix. The set rounds out with classic sing‑along moments—Sugar Magnolia, Not Fade Away into Goin' Down The Road Feeling Bad, and a rollicking One More Saturday Night—that keep the energy cooking to the very end. While the soundboard capture is a bit muffled and Keith can be overly forward, it remains the most complete source of this high‑energy performance.",
